Here is an example C++ program that uses the pigpio library to control GPIO pin 12 with hardware PWM on a Raspberry Pi 4B:
```
#include <pigpio.h>

int main()
{
    // Initialize the pigpio library
    if (gpioInitialise() < 0)
    {
        // pigpio initialization failed
        return 1;
    }

    // Set GPIO pin 12 to be a hardware PWM output
    gpioSetMode(12, PI_OUTPUT);

    // Set the PWM frequency to 50 Hz
    gpioSetPWMfrequency(12, 50);

    // Set the PWM duty cycle to 50%
    gpioSetPWMrange(12, 100);
    gpioPWM(12, 50);

    // Wait for a few seconds
    gpioDelay(3000);

    // Reset the PWM duty cycle to 0%
    gpioPWM(12, 0);

    // Release resources and terminate the pigpio library
    gpioTerminate();

    return 0;
}
```
This program initializes the pigpio library, sets GPIO pin 12 to be a hardware PWM output, sets the PWM frequency to 50 Hz, sets the PWM duty cycle to 50%, waits for a few seconds, and then resets the PWM duty cycle to 0%.

