Here is an example of how you can move a 2D sprite in a circle with variable speed control, an activator, and a distance offset from the origin using UniRx in Unity:
```
using UnityEngine;
using System.Collections;
using UniRx;

public class CircleMover : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] private float speed = 1.0f;
    [SerializeField] private bool activate = false;
    [SerializeField] private float distance = 1.0f;

    private void Start()
    {
        Observable.EveryUpdate()
            .Where(_ => activate)
            .Subscribe(_ => 
            {
                float x = Mathf.Sin(Time.time * speed) * distance;
                float y = Mathf.Cos(Time.time * speed) * distance;
                transform.position = new Vector3(x, y, 0);
            });
    }
}
```
In this example, the `activate`, `speed` and `distance` variables are private and serialized fields that can be set in the Unity editor. When `activate` is set to true, the sprite's position is updated every frame to move in a circle with distance offset from the origin. The `speed` variable can be set to control the speed of the movement and `distance` variable is used to control the distance of the circle movement from origin.

