```
In both examples, the `getBlockTimestamp()` function retrieves the block information for the specified block number using either ethers.js or web3.js and returns the block timestamp in seconds. When you call this function and pass in the appropriate provider or web3 instance along with the block number, you'll get the block timestamp in seconds directly.

