It's not uncommon for the 'name' property of a device to be null when using the react-native-ble-manager library. There could be several reasons why this happens:

1. The BLE device is not broadcasting its name. Some devices do not include their name in the advertisement data, so you might not get the name property when scanning.
2. The device name is not in the advertisement data, but it can be found in the GATT service. In this case, you'll need to connect to the device and read the name from the GATT service. The standard GATT service for device information is 0x1800, and the characteristic for the device name is 0x2A00.

Here's an example of how you could try to retrieve the device name from the GATT service:
```javascript
import BleManager from 'react-native-ble-manager';

async function getDeviceName(peripheralId) {
  try {
    // Connect to the device
    await BleManager.connect(peripheralId);

    // Discover device services and characteristics
    const deviceInfo = await BleManager.retrieveServices(peripheralId);

    // Look for the device information service (0x1800)
    const deviceInfoService = deviceInfo.services.find(
      (service) => service.toUpperCase() === '1800'
    );

    if (deviceInfoService) {
      // Read the device name characteristic (0x2A00)
      const deviceName = await BleManager.read(
        peripheralId,
        '1800',
        '2A00'
      );

      // Decode the device name from bytes to a string
      const decodedDeviceName = new TextDecoder('utf-8').decode(
        new Uint8Array(deviceName)
      );

      console.log('Device Name:', decodedDeviceName);
      return decodedDeviceName;
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.log('Error:', error);
  } finally {
    // Disconnect from the device
    BleManager.disconnect(peripheralId);
  }
}
```
1. It's also possible that there's an issue with your react-native-ble-manager library or your React Native environment. Ensure you have the latest version of the library installed and check if there are any known issues on the GitHub repository.

Remember to handle null names gracefully in your application to account for devices that don't provide a name.

